# `power::Grid::base_power`

[Back to `power::Grid`](../Grid.md)

The three-phase apparent-power base in volt-amperes.

## Signature

```cpp
double power::Grid::base_power() const noexcept;
```

## What It Does

Returns the apparent-power base that converts per-unit powers to watts. It is the `power` field of [`base`](base.md); use it when you want only that number.

## Returns

The power base in VA.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A 100 MVA base.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace power = pluss::subsp::eng::power;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series vec(std::vector<double> v) { return pluss::series::make(v); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  power::Net net;
  net.base = {100e6, 230e3};
  net.buses.kind = {power::BusKind::Slack, power::BusKind::PQ};
  net.buses.p = vec({0.0, -0.5});
  net.buses.q = vec({0.0, -0.2});
  net.buses.vm = vec({1.0, 1.0});
  net.buses.va = vec({0.0, 0.0});
  net.lines.from = {0};
  net.lines.to = {1};
  net.lines.r = vec({0.01});
  net.lines.x = vec({0.1});
  const power::Grid obj = power::make(net);
  out.writeln("base power (MVA) =", obj.base_power() / 1e6);
}
```

### Example 2

The same two buses on a 50 MVA, 115 kV base.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace power = pluss::subsp::eng::power;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series vec(std::vector<double> v) { return pluss::series::make(v); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  power::Net net;
  net.base = {50e6, 115e3};
  net.buses.kind = {power::BusKind::Slack, power::BusKind::PQ};
  net.buses.p = vec({0.0, -0.5});
  net.buses.q = vec({0.0, -0.2});
  net.buses.vm = vec({1.0, 1.0});
  net.buses.va = vec({0.0, 0.0});
  net.lines.from = {0};
  net.lines.to = {1};
  net.lines.r = vec({0.01});
  net.lines.x = vec({0.1});
  const power::Grid obj = power::make(net);
  out.writeln("base power (MVA) =", obj.base_power() / 1e6);
}
```

### Example 3

The three-bus grid uses the same 100 MVA base.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace power = pluss::subsp::eng::power;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series vec(std::vector<double> v) { return pluss::series::make(v); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  power::Net net;
  net.base = {100e6, 230e3};
  net.buses.kind = {power::BusKind::Slack, power::BusKind::PV, power::BusKind::PQ};
  net.buses.p = vec({0.0, -0.2, -0.5});
  net.buses.q = vec({0.0, 0.0, -0.2});
  net.buses.vm = vec({1.04, 1.02, 1.0});
  net.buses.va = vec({0.0, 0.0, 0.0});
  net.gens.bus = {1};
  net.gens.p = vec({0.6});
  net.gens.q = vec({0.0});
  net.lines.from = {0, 1, 0};
  net.lines.to = {1, 2, 2};
  net.lines.r = vec({0.01, 0.02, 0.015});
  net.lines.x = vec({0.1, 0.2, 0.25});
  net.lines.charge = vec({0.02, 0.05, 0.04});
  const power::Grid obj = power::make(net);
  out.writeln("base power (MVA) =", obj.base_power() / 1e6);
}
```

